     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Block h1_1:escalate and h1_2:pivot. Blocking h1_1:escalate cuts h2_0:access, which removes both h4_0:access and h4_3:access. It also cuts h2_1:access and h3_2:pivot. Blocking h1_2:pivot cuts h2_3:escalate (an AND step that needs it) and h3_1:escalate. That leaves h4_2:reach with no reachable parent, so crown:obtain has none either. One block is not enough: the path through h2_0:access to h4_0:access and the path through h1_2:pivot and h3_1:escalate to h4_2:reach share no blockable step, since edge2:reach is a foothold.\"}"
